0 findings; 0 on their lines. Reply in a comment's thread to answer it.

### Summary

I found nothing to flag in this part, and I read every file in it. The deferred colour upgrade now has its own `pendingColorUpgrade` marker. On reconnect it writes only if the folder still holds the old Default in rose, and otherwise adopts the folder's file. An edit made while the folder was away still wins. Choosing the folder the workspace already points at now returns early with no side effects, and the probe afterwards still runs. A `pendingInit` workspace can now be repointed to a folder with Kaipu items and no identity. The renderer now handles rejected create, edit and relocate calls with \"uncertain\" messages, in both the dialog and the Settings toast. The tests match what their names claim. Of the open threads, three of the earlier-round ones on this part's files are now addressed in the code. Two of the Change folder… ones (`pendingInit` moved folder, capture drop) are still open. In the `pendingInit` thread, a moved folder holding a different workspace id is still refused as `different`, although `availability` would adopt that id. The capture-drop thread concerns `switch-transaction.ts`, which this part does not change.

